WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.080
Spiralling horrors, a gender-bent riff&nbsp;
on Shakespeare… and a whole series about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:10.880
camping? Here's a few upcoming titles that&nbsp;
anime fans are looking forward to in 2022.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:17.520
Anime and horror fans got some very welcome news&nbsp;
in October 2019, when Adult Swim announced it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:23.600
turning Junji Ito's terrifying masterpiece&nbsp;
"Uzumaki" into a four-part miniseries. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:29.280
beloved late-90s manga received a live-action&nbsp;
adaptation in 2000 that got mixed reviews,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:35.360
but if anyone can pull off an animated take on&nbsp;
Ito's supernatural tale, it's Hiroshi Nagahama.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:40.960
Nagahama, best known for turning the trippy&nbsp;
horror manga "Mushishi" into a highly-rated hit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:46.800
has big plans for "Uzumaki." In the first teaser&nbsp;
for the show, Nagahama stated his artistic vision:

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:50.880
"[I wanted to make] something that scares&nbsp;
people and makes them laugh and that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:55.280
they'll watch over and over. That's&nbsp;
the kind of work I want this to be."

00:00:55.280 --> 00:01:00.640
Nagahama's promises got fans of Ito's manga&nbsp;
excited, but the original 2020 release date&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:05.040
came and went without a premiere. In&nbsp;
2021, Adult Swim confirmed that "Uzumaki"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:09.600
was still in progress and would drop&nbsp;
the following year. Nagahama told fans,

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:14.880
"I feel truly apologetic for the delay and&nbsp;
ask for your patience just a little more."

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:18.400
"Uzumaki" — which translates&nbsp;
to "spiral" — takes place in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:23.440
small Japanese town where a supernatural&nbsp;
curse is wreaking havoc. Production I.G,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:27.200
the studio responsible for "Ghost in&nbsp;
the Shell," has been making strong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:31.520
efforts to adapt Ito's art style to&nbsp;
the screen as faithfully as possible.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:36.160
Funimation teamed up with Fox to&nbsp;
release 2018's "Dragon Ball Super:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:42.000
Broly" in theaters across 18 different countries,&nbsp;
and it proved to be a wise move. The film raked in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:48.160
over $115 million at the worldwide box&nbsp;
office and earned rave reviews from critics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:51.680
becoming a hit even with viewers&nbsp;
unfamiliar with the franchise.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:56.800
There's been a renewed interest in all things&nbsp;
"Dragon Ball" since the sequel series "Dragon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:02.400
Ball Super" began airing in 2015, and the&nbsp;
fanbase is now bigger than ever. Fans who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:06.960
grew up watching the original '80s anime are&nbsp;
now sharing it with their children, creating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:12.400
what Funimation's Mitchel Berger calls, quote,&nbsp;
"multi-generational appeal." This was reflected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:18.000
in the rapturous response to "Dragon Ball Super:&nbsp;
Broly," which gave the titular Saiyan a new and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:23.680
improved origin story. It was so well-received,&nbsp;
in fact, that series creator Akira Toriyama&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:30.080
confirmed that a new film, "Dragon Ball Super:&nbsp;
Super Hero," was in the pipeline for 2022.

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:31.040
"It's about time!"

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:35.920
Toriyama hyped up the film on the&nbsp;
official "Dragon Ball" website, writing,

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:40.880
"Just like the previous movie, I'm heavily&nbsp;
leading the story and dialogue production.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:46.000
I really shouldn't talk too much about the&nbsp;
plot yet, but be prepared for some extreme&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:50.480
and entertaining bouts, which may&nbsp;
feature an unexpected character."

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:56.000
The film's title and updated character designs&nbsp;
were revealed at Comic-Con at Home 2021.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:03.920
What's cooler than a guy with a chainsaw?&nbsp;
A guy who is a chainsaw. Tatsuki Fujimoto's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:09.120
action fantasy "Chainsaw Man" made waves&nbsp;
when it hit shelves in December 2018.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.680
MAPPA — the studio behind behind "Dorohedoro" and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:16.480
"Jujutsu Kaisen" — was quick to take on the&nbsp;
challenge of adapting the high-octane manga.

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:22.000
Denji is a devil hunter buried in debt,&nbsp;
barely scraping by with his devil-dog Pochita.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:26.240
When a job gone wrong ends with the&nbsp;
yakuza literally backstabbing him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:31.040
Denji makes a deal with Pochita that&nbsp;
allows him to be reborn as a human-devil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:36.000
hybrid. By pulling the cord on his chest,&nbsp;
Denji can become the Chainsaw Devil:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.680
a monster with multiple chainsaws&nbsp;
emerging from his head and arms.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:45.920
Known for its brutal fights and dark humor, the&nbsp;
"Chainsaw Man" manga won the 2020 Shogakukan&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:50.240
award for Best Shonen. While an exact&nbsp;
release date has yet to be determined,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:56.480
a recent trailer confirms that fans can expect to&nbsp;
see the bloody affair on the small screen in 2022.

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:03.200
The hit 2020 anime "Moriarty the Patriot" offered&nbsp;
a new take on a classic literary character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:07.200
and another radically different version&nbsp;
of a famous villain is slated to hit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:12.080
the small screen in 2022 — only this&nbsp;
time, it's one that actually existed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:17.200
Aya Kanno's manga series "Requiem of&nbsp;
the Rose King" follows a gender-fluid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:21.440
version of Richard the Third, one of&nbsp;
the most hated monarchs in history.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:26.480
The show takes place in the period known as the&nbsp;
War of the Roses, a 30-year conflict between the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:31.280
noble houses of York and Lancaster. When the story&nbsp;
begins, Richard's father is closing in on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:36.880
throne, but it's not to be: The Duke of York has&nbsp;
the crown — and his life — snatched away before he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:43.040
can claim it. The loss of his father hits Richard&nbsp;
hard. The bloody conflict rages on, however, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:49.680
with his beloved dad now gone, Richard's thoughts&nbsp;
turn to revenge and, ultimately, the throne.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:52.720
Loosely based on the classic&nbsp;
Shakespeare play "Richard III,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:58.320
the manga debuted in Monthly Princess magazine&nbsp;
in 2013 and is still going strong today. Known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:03.120
for being full of unexpected twists and&nbsp;
turns, "Requiem of the Rose King" will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:08.080
no doubt make for a fascinating anime&nbsp;
series when it drops in January 2022.

00:05:08.501 --> 00:05:13.520
"The Rising of the Shield Hero" was&nbsp;
one of the most popular anime of 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:17.760
but it was also one of the most controversial.&nbsp;
On paper, it's just a standard isekai — a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:22.720
fantasy subgenre in which the protagonist is&nbsp;
suddenly transported to a strange new world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:26.560
It's difficult for new isekai shows to&nbsp;
stand out from the incredibly large crowd,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:32.080
but "The Rising of the Shield Hero" managed&nbsp;
to do so in an incredibly bold and risky way:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:36.640
after arriving in his fantasy world, the&nbsp;
protagonist is falsely accused of sexual assault.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:41.440
Socially inept otaku Naofumi Iwatani is one&nbsp;
of four regular people summoned to the kingdom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:46.000
of Melromarc to save it from impending&nbsp;
doom. Dubbed the Four Cardinal Heroes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:50.320
each receives a legendary weapon to&nbsp;
help them in their quest — Naofumi's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:54.880
weapon being a shield. When his training&nbsp;
partner betrays him with a treacherous lie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:59.760
Naofumi becomes an outcast, setting out to&nbsp;
combat the Waves of Calamity on his own.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:04.160
Some people took issue with the show's use of&nbsp;
a sexual assault accusation as a plot device,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:08.480
but fans have been clamoring for a second&nbsp;
season ever since the first one wrapped.

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:13.600
The fact that "A Couple of Cuckoos" has become&nbsp;
one of the most anticipated anime of 2022&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:17.200
is quite remarkable, considering how&nbsp;
new the manga that it's based on is.

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:22.080
Written and illustrated by Miki Yoshikawa,&nbsp;
"A Couple of Cuckoos" is massive in Japan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:26.960
Two volumes of the cutesy rom-com were sold&nbsp;
every second during the height of its popularity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:32.480
and fans can't wait to see how director&nbsp;
Yoshiyuki Shirahata handles the story.

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:37.360
As the teaser trailer for the show reveals, "A&nbsp;
Couple of Cuckoos" is a love story about a shy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:42.080
boy and an internet-famous girl. Introverted&nbsp;
high school student Nagi Umino is on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:46.400
way to meet his biological parents for the&nbsp;
first time when he encounters Erika Amano,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:52.320
a social media star trying to escape an arranged&nbsp;
marriage. She proposes that Nagi become her fake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:57.200
boyfriend so she doesn't have to go through with&nbsp;
it, and he reluctantly agrees. They soon discover&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:02.640
that Nagi is actually her intended husband after&nbsp;
all — they were accidentally switched as babies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:07.040
and the parents believe a wedding is the&nbsp;
best way they can be a proper family.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:11.600
Unfortunately for them, Nagi has his&nbsp;
eye on someone else, and chaos ensues.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:16.720
Another show that was pushed back to&nbsp;
2022 because of the coronavirus pandemic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:20.000
"Spriggan" is a collaboration&nbsp;
between Netflix and David Production.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:26.400
For those unfamiliar with the title, "Spriggan" is&nbsp;
a shonen sci-fi manga that ran from 1989 to 1996&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:31.520
and got a movie adaptation in 1998. “Spriggan”&nbsp;
takes place in an alternate reality version of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:36.560
the Cold War, in which mankind has discovered&nbsp;
the existence of advanced tech hidden by an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:42.080
ancient civilization. Making sure these gadgets&nbsp;
don't fall into the wrong hands is Yu Ominae,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:47.440
a member of an elite unit that takes on militias&nbsp;
and assorted bad guys with ulterior motives.

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:50.480
Netflix has already dropped a couple&nbsp;
of teaser trailers for "Spriggan,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:55.920
and they look great. David Production&nbsp;
knows all about flamboyance — this is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:59.520
the studio behind "JoJo's Bizarre&nbsp;
Adventure," after all — but they're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:04.320
wisely keeping things sleek and simple with&nbsp;
this particular project. Hiroshi Kobayashi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:09.760
who has directed episodes of "Kiznaiver" and&nbsp;
"Tiger &amp; Bunny," is overseeing the action.

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:12.160
"Well, you can color me impressed."

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:17.520
At a glance, "Made in Abyss" looks like the kind&nbsp;
of show you could comfortably watch with children,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:22.320
but the 2017 adventure series is&nbsp;
far from a family-friendly affair.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:25.760
Based on Akihito Tsukushi's&nbsp;
manga series of the same name,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:30.640
"Made in Abyss" follows an orphan girl named&nbsp;
Riko who lives in a town built around a giant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:36.720
gaping hole referred to as — you guessed it —&nbsp;
the Abyss. All manner of strange artifacts and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:42.080
creatures are said to be found inside, though&nbsp;
few are brave enough to explore its depths.

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:46.560
Those who enter the hole are known as Cave&nbsp;
Raiders, one of whom was Riko's mother. Although&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:51.120
she seemingly vanished during an expedition,&nbsp;
it turns out she may not be gone after all:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:54.880
when Riko finds a message from her mother&nbsp;
urging her to meet her in the Abyss,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:59.120
she decides that it's time to explore it for&nbsp;
herself with the help of a new robot friend.

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:04.560
Season 2 of "Made in Abyss'' was announced&nbsp;
in 2019, and a film entitled "Dawn of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:08.720
Deep Soul" dropped the following year.&nbsp;
The story is set to continue in 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:12.640
when the second season — officially titled&nbsp;
"Made in Abyss: The Sun Blazes Upon the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:17.600
Golden City" — will come to air. Plot details&nbsp;
are being kept mostly under wraps for now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:20.720
but at least one previously&nbsp;
unseen character will appear:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:25.840
Manga readers will no doubt recognize the fluffy&nbsp;
white arms of Faputa, Princess of the Narehate.

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:33.200
The global phenomenon that was the "Attack on&nbsp;
Titan" manga came to an end when the final chapter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:38.400
shipped in Bessatsu Shonen Magazine in summer&nbsp;
2021. For anime viewers, however, the journey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:43.840
doesn't reach its conclusion until 2022, when the&nbsp;
second part of the fourth and final season is set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.840 --> 00:09:48.400
to air. "Attack on Titan" fans became worried&nbsp;
when it was revealed that Wit Studio would no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:54.000
longer produce the show after Season 3, but&nbsp;
MAPPA stepped in and exceeded expectations.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:58.080
Season 3 of "Attack on Titan" ended&nbsp;
on a rare high note for our heroes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:02.880
who got to see the ocean for the first time,&nbsp;
but things were far from rosy when we caught&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:07.280
up with them in "Attack on Titan: The Final&nbsp;
Season Part 1." There's a four year time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.280 --> 00:10:12.560
jump between the seasons, and protagonist&nbsp;
Eren Yeager isn't the same man he once was.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:17.440
Noticeably older, the veteran of the Survey&nbsp;
Corps has been worn down by the rigors of war,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:22.560
as have his comrades. There's trouble with the&nbsp;
country across the sea: Marley is at war with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:27.600
the Eldians, the descendants of the first Titan.&nbsp;
Eren also has an old acquaintance to worry about:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:33.600
the Part 1 finale ended just as he was about&nbsp;
to face former friend Reiner Braun in battle.

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:38.480
"Attack on Titan: The Final Season Part&nbsp;
2" will begin on January 9th, 2022.

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:43.760
A live-action movie adaptation of the&nbsp;
original anime series "Tiger &amp; Bunny"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:47.440
was announced in 2015, with Ron&nbsp;
Howard attached as a producer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:51.040
Despite the fact that superhero&nbsp;
movies have only grown in popularity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:55.840
there's been little movement since. However,&nbsp;
fans of "Tiger &amp; Bunny" need not despair:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.840 --> 00:11:00.800
their decade-long wait for a second season of&nbsp;
the original show is soon to become a reality.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:06.000
Sunrise, the studio behind the original "Tiger &amp;&nbsp;
Bunny," has confirmed that the highly-anticipated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.000 --> 00:11:11.440
follow-up season, entitled "Tiger &amp; Bunny&nbsp;
2," will come to air at some point in 2022.

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:15.200
“Tiger &amp; Bunny” takes place in a&nbsp;
far-future city called Stern Bild,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:20.720
which is rife with both crime and superheroes.&nbsp;
Wearing costumes plastered in sponsors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.720 --> 00:11:25.680
the vigilantes of Stern Bild take part in&nbsp;
a show called "Hero TV," competing against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:29.600
each other by earning points for every&nbsp;
crime they stop. Whoever earns the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:35.120
points is crowned the "King of Heroes" — but&nbsp;
not all of them care about fame and prestige.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:40.960
We follow veteran superhero Kotetsu "Wild Tiger"&nbsp;
Kaburagi and his rookie partner Barnaby "Bunny"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.960 --> 00:11:45.840
Brooks Jr., two men who have very different&nbsp;
opinions about what it means to be a hero.

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:52.880
Influential '80s anime "Captain Tsubasa" got a&nbsp;
brand new season in 2018, reigniting interest in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:57.840
soccer shows. In 2022, another fictional Japanese&nbsp;
player will make the leap from the pages of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.840 --> 00:12:03.280
manga to the small screen: Aoi Ashito, the&nbsp;
protagonist of Yugo Kobayashi's "Ao Ashi".

00:12:03.280 --> 00:12:08.000
Aoi has plenty of raw talent, but needs some&nbsp;
work if he's going to make it all the way to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:13.280
the J League, Japan's premier soccer division.&nbsp;
Luckily, coach Tatsuya Fukuda is willing to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.280 --> 00:12:18.320
put the work in: after recognizing his potential,&nbsp;
the former pro invites Aoi to a training camp for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:24.000
Tokyo City Esperion FC's youth team. Like all the&nbsp;
other animated soccer stars that came before him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:27.760
Aoi revolutionizes the sport in&nbsp;
Japan, but what makes "Ao Ashi"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:32.720
different is that it's relatively new, and&nbsp;
therefore much in tune with the modern game.

00:12:32.720 --> 00:12:38.000
The action in "Captain Tsubasa" is often so&nbsp;
exaggerated that it barely resembles real soccer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:42.560
but "Ao Ashi" takes the sport seriously, with&nbsp;
characters learning formations and executing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:47.600
plays that you would see in an actual real-life&nbsp;
game. It's the manga that soccer fans had been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:53.360
waiting for, and the anime adaptation is dropping&nbsp;
at the perfect time — it's scheduled for release&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:58.880
during the Spring 2022 season, meaning it will&nbsp;
be on air in the run up to the FIFA World Cup.

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:06.080
From calligraphy to mineralogy to fishing and&nbsp;
ballroom dancing, there's an anime for just about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.080 --> 00:13:10.880
every hobby. Based on the slice-of-life manga&nbsp;
of the same name, "Laid-Back Camp" caters to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:15.280
lovers of camping, following a group of friends&nbsp;
who travel to different sites across Japan.

00:13:15.280 --> 00:13:20.480
It's a delightfully simple story that made for&nbsp;
a charming anime when studio C-Station adapted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:25.360
it for the small screen in 2018. There's also&nbsp;
a live action TV remake for fans to check out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:30.400
but what they really want is more anime — and&nbsp;
that's exactly what they're getting in 2022.

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:34.800
As the promotional poster reveals, the "Laid-Back&nbsp;
Camp" girls are returning for an anime movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:39.240
along with the creators that made the anime&nbsp;
series such a success. Screenwriters Jin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:44.640
Tanaka and Mutsumi Ito are back, as is director&nbsp;
Yoshiaki Kyogoku , whose work on "Laid-Back Camp"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:49.600
earned him an award at the Tokyo Anime Film&nbsp;
Festival. Kyogoku told Anime News Network,

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:52.720
"I like to think that the award&nbsp;
went to the show and not to me.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:57.920
While the show was good, it's not mine. It was&nbsp;
all the staff's hard work that made it possible. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.920 --> 00:14:03.760
would like to think that the award came to me as a&nbsp;
representative of the show and not me personally."

00:14:03.760 --> 00:14:06.080
